CORE broken-libstdcxx16 libstdcxx
chrono.cpp
--cpp20 --object-bits 12
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ duration: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
dropped the body
could not fully type-check
--
libstdc++ 13 <chrono>: `12h' (chrono_literals) is fixed
(cpp11_user_defined_literal_call_forms), as are __check_overflow (the
_Number_help recursion, cpp11_alias_template_in_recursive_class_template)
and default_delete<time_zone::_Impl>::operator() (bits/unique_ptr.h:93),
instantiated for the incomplete _Impl by time_zone's unused defaulted special
members (cpp98_implicit_default_constructor_defined_only_when_odr_used).
g++ 13 accepts this program, and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
broken-libstdcxx16: with libstdc++ 16 (16-20260315), _M_reserve and _M_span
of <format>'s _Seq_sink lose their bodies (KNOWNBUG
cpp20_hidden_friend_spaceship_template_alias_return_type).  The earlier
drops of __do_vformat_to and __get_leap_second_info and the
--validate-goto-model type mismatch no longer occur (checked 2026-10-26).
